note: 
  --> sequence.wipple:5:11
  |
5 | box : Box "abc"
  |           -----

`"abc"` is a string literal.

This means `"abc"` is a `String`, `Box "abc"` is a `Box String`, `box` is a `Box String`, and 2 others.

note: 
  --> sequence.wipple:6:14
  |
6 | positive? : (n :: Number) -> _
  |              -

`n` is annotated as a `Number`.

This means `n` is a `Number`.

note: 
  --> sequence.wipple:7:2
  |
7 | (filter positive?) box
  |  ------

`filter` keeps the elements in `box` that satisfy `positive?`.

This means `"abc"` must have the same type as `n`.

This means `_` is a `Boolean`.

This uses `instance (As-Sequence (Box String) String)`.

error: 
  --> sequence.wipple:5:11
  |
5 | box : Box "abc"
  |           ^^^^^

`"abc"` is a `String` or a `Number`, but it can only be one of these.

